ROMulus
=======

ROMulus is a fork of RomM (https://github.com/rommapp/romm), which is licensed
under the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3 (see LICENSE).

This file records the modification, as section 5 of that licence asks: the
software has been changed, and the changes are described here and in the
repository's history.

What the fork adds
------------------
A plugin system: a plugin is a manifest on disk ($ROMM_BASE_PATH/plugins/<id>/
plugin.json) that adds actions which open a URL, and panels that show data an
external source answers about a game — for example, what emulator runs it well
on a given handheld. Plugins declare their own settings, which the server
validates and stores beside the manifest. There is a curated index of plugins
(jkoehler11/romm-plugins) that an administrator can browse and install from.

No plugin runs code on the server. A plugin can only cause the server to read a
URL the plugin supplied, and only a public one.

Where the change lives
----------------------
The plugin system is additive, so that this fork can keep merging upstream:

  backend/handler/plugin_*.py        manifests, panels, settings, option search
  backend/endpoints/plugins.py       the plugin routes
  backend/endpoints/responses/plugin.py
  backend/utils/context.py           a shared, public-only HTTP client
  frontend/src/views/Settings/Plugins.vue
  frontend/src/components/Settings/Plugin*.vue
  frontend/src/components/shared/PluginSlot.vue
  docs/PLUGINS.md

Edits to existing files are small and marked by their call sites: the router
include in backend/main.py, the Play button and action row, the settings
sidebar, and the i18n bundle.

Continuous integration was replaced as well: RomM's workflows are written for
RomM's repository and its secrets, so this fork runs .github/workflows/
romulus-ci.yml and romulus-image.yml instead, and disables the originals in the
GitHub settings rather than deleting them.

